Gnucap Models, "nonfree" section

Here we store model code that lacks the four freedoms. In most cases this
means that we have no permission to distribute modified copies, for any
purpose. The details can be a minefield and you should consult a lawyer or
contact the respective authors if you wish to make serious use of the
contents provided.

The section name characterises the license situation of the models therein,
not their technical quality or their usefulness. See [1] for why the former is
considered to be of higher importance. The term "nonfree" was copied from the
Debian project, which runs an archive with this name (actually, "non-free")
serving a similar purpose.

[1] https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/open-source-misses-the-point.html
